{
  "description": "an every handler body runs in the environment captured at REGISTRATION, not the one current when it fires. The handler is registered inside setup and fires from the top-level wait, after setup has already returned - so :v exists only in the registration environment. Printing 7 is therefore only possible if that environment was captured and used; resolving against the firing-time scope instead raises ol-undefined-var, since :v is not bound at top level. This pins the capture of the environment itself, which is a different and weaker property than capturing VALUES: the runtime snapshots nothing and creates no fresh bindings, which is why issue #821's loop case is still open. The when kind has when-start-captures-registration-scope, but that handler fires synchronously during registration and so cannot distinguish the two scopes; this fixture can, because the procedure has returned",
